{
  "statement": "A query is built from the words of the dump being answered and nothing else, plus their country when the fact depends on where they are. No date it worked out, no name from a note, no clause of its own. When the fact needs a country and none is known, the reply is Not sure. rather than an answer for the wrong country. From inside a thread that puts them somewhere else, an answering turn asks which country and picks neither.",
  "why": "A query is the one thing that leaves, so it carries only what they typed. The bound fails closed: a refused query costs an answer, never a wrong one. A bank holiday with no country has no answer, and the search will quietly answer for the United States if allowed.",
  "sources": [
    "016 AC-24 (a poisoned note cannot reach a query)",
    "016: what may go into a query",
    "018 AC-1 to AC-3 (the country question)",
    "worker.py: _from_the_dump",
    "answer.md: Use only words that are in their question, plus their country"
  ],
